  "details": "Currently, users must manually set their AFK (Away From Keyboard) status in VRChat, which often leads to forgotten status changes and confusion. As a result, friends may attempt to visit or invite users who are actually AFK, wasting time and effort.\n\nI propose an automatic AFK detection system that visually indicates when a user is inactive for a certain period. This could include options like:\n\n・Automatically changing to an AFK animation or idle state.\n\n・Displaying an \"AFK\" label on the user's nameplate (especially visible in the user list or launchpad menu).\n\n・Dimming the user's nameplate to visually show inactivity.\n\nThis would make it easier for others to identify AFK users and avoid unnecessary invitations or visits. A setting should be available to turn this feature off for privacy, but it should be enabled by default.\n\nThis small change would greatly improve communication and efficiency in social interactions on VRChat.",
